Changes made by the kiln project (Apache 2.0 §4(b))

Source: https://github.com/BinomialLLC/basis_universal, commit 9bebe16726b3a61c8c213eeee3b7cffb462ef34e
(v2.50). The text above is that commit's NOTICE file, unchanged.

basisu_bc7f.cpp and basisu_bc7f.h are modified extracts of transcoder/basisu_transcoder.cpp,
basisu_transcoder_internal.h, basisu_transcoder_uastc.h, basisu_containers.h and basisu.h.
The changes:

- Only the BC7 encoder (namespace bc7f), the BC7 decoder it calls (the first namespace bc7u) and
  the helpers and tables they use are kept. The ASTC packers of bc7f, fast_pack_bc7_auto_rgb(),
  the perf-stat functions, fast_floorf_int() and bc7u's determine_bc7_mode*() functions are removed.
- The code is inside namespace kiln_bc7f (so basist becomes kiln_bc7f::basist, basisu becomes
  kiln_bc7f::basisu), which keeps it apart from a full Basis Universal in the same program.
- The #if BASISU_BC7F_PERF_STATS and #if BASISU_BC7F_USE_SSE41 blocks are removed (both are 0
  upstream). popcount32() and pop16() use std::popcount instead of compiler intrinsics.
- color_rgba loses its color32 conversions and its eNoClamp constructor.
- g_bc7_mode_5_optimal_endpoints is static here; bc7f::init() fills it with the BC7 777 loop of
  transcoder_init_bc7_mode5(), which basisu_transcoder_init() runs upstream.
- basisu_bc7f.h is new: the bc7f flag constants (same values), init(), and
  fast_pack_bc7_auto_rgba() taking 64 RGBA8 bytes.

The encoder's arithmetic is unchanged. Its output was checked byte-identical to the upstream
transcoder's bc7f::fast_pack_bc7_auto_rgba() for the Fast, Default, PartiallyAnalytical and
NonAnalytical flag sets.
